+/// The EPOC+ vendor service, which uses an entirely different identifier
+/// family from the `1100-d102` services above.
+///
+/// Verified against an EPOC+ (firmware 0x0633) on 16 Nov 2026 by enumerating
+/// its GATT table directly. It exposes four characteristics: `…2f41` notifies
+/// encrypted EEG at roughly 257 notifications a second, `…2f42` notifies
+/// motion at roughly 32, `…2f43` is writable and notifying, and `…2f44` reads
+/// back a six-byte status word.
+///
+/// Notifications begin as soon as they are subscribed to — no start-stream
+/// command is needed — and a 32-byte packet arrives as 20 + 12 at the default
+/// MTU, which the decode pipeline already reassembles.
+///
+/// Without this service listed, a grant reaches none of the above and the
+/// connection fails with "no accessible primary services on this device".
+pub(crate) const EMOTIV_SERVICE_EPOC_PLUS: Uuid =
+    Uuid::from_u128(0x81072f40_9f3d_11e3_a9dc_0002a5d5c51b);
+
 /// Every vendor service a headset may expose. Named in each grant, because
 /// `get_characteristics` only reaches the services a grant lists.
-pub(crate) const EMOTIV_SERVICES: [Uuid; 4] = [
+pub(crate) const EMOTIV_SERVICES: [Uuid; 5] = [
     EMOTIV_DATA_SERVICE,
     EMOTIV_CONTROL_SERVICE,
     EMOTIV_SERVICE_1102,
     EMOTIV_SERVICE_1103,
+    EMOTIV_SERVICE_EPOC_PLUS,
 ];
 
